also hold an imported transcript for analysis.
}
\details{
\code{\link[=run_focus_group]{run_focus_group()}} accepts phase counts or ordered moderator instructions
and returns a structured \code{focus_group_result}. For direct construction,
create \link{FGAgent} objects and a \link{ConversationFlow}, then pass them to
\link{FocusGroup}. Built-in flows are constructed with
\code{\link[=create_conversation_flow]{create_conversation_flow()}}.

\code{\link[=create_agents]{create_agents()}}, \code{\link[=create_agents_from_data]{create_agents_from_data()}}, and
\code{\link[=create_agents_from_survey]{create_agents_from_survey()}} construct agents from direct personas or
respondent records. \code{\link[=focus_group_from_transcript]{focus_group_from_transcript()}} imports an existing
transcript without generating new turns.

Model calls require an explicit \code{config} built with \code{\link[LLMR:llm_config]{LLMR::llm_config()}}.
The high-level runner and agent constructors accept \code{.runner}, an optional
function used instead of live model calls. It uses a request and response
data-frame format.
Descriptive analysis of an imported transcript does not require a provider
call. Model summaries and thematic analysis are opt-in through an explicit
\code{config}.
